  "summary": "Messages queue cleared: all 13 items closed under RBC-RX-05.\n\n- pt-0026 Hayes (2 messages, same request): lisinopril 20 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. The 10/5 potassium of 6.1 came from a hemolyzed sample, so it doesn't count; decided on the valid 4.6 from 4/14 (BMP within 12 months). Repeat BMP ordered. Patient replied to.\n- pt-0027 Odum: lisinopril 10 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. The outside St. Brigid potassium of 5.9 (collected 8/27) was also hemolyzed, so it doesn't count; valid potassium 4.5 from the 1/20 BMP. Repeat BMP ordered. Amlodipine 5 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (§4, visit 1/20). Patient replied to.\n- pt-0028 Park: metformin not refilled. Her most recent valid eGFR is 39: the lab corrected the 7/20 result (creatinine 1.62, eGFR 39, previously reported as 1.28 and 51). The 7/20 progress note's plan to continue metformin used the old values. Urgent review task for you, focused on mr-00287. Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply, no refills, because the last BMP (10/2/2025) is over 12 months old; BMP ordered. Patient replied to.\n- pt-0029 Brooks: lisinopril 20 mg not refilled. Creatinine rose 37.8% (0.90 to 1.24) within 4 weeks of the 9/21 dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. ASAP review task for you, focused on mr-00291. She says she ran out on 10/20. Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: 30-day supply, no refills (eGFR 54, but her last HbA1c was 4/14/2026, more than 6 months ago); HbA1c ordered. Patient replied to, with advice on when to seek urgent care.\n- pt-0030 Price (3 messages; the patient's and pharmacy's metformin requests handled as one): lisinopril 20 mg renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (BMP 10/6, potassium 5.2, creatinine up 23.6% after the dose increase, under the 30% limit). Metformin 1000 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (eGFR 65; outside HbA1c 8/19/2026). Patient replied to.\n- pt-0031 Webb: metformin 500 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error (mislabelled sample); valid eGFR is 92, and HbA1c is from 9/28. Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply, no refills (last BMP 10/20/2025, over 12 months old); BMP ordered. Patient replied to.\n\nEach new prescription replaces the patient's previous active one.",
